Notebook[{
Cell["Shallow water, DE4plus ansatz", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"aeedb676-8a0a-477a-9bb0-eb03f1f4395b"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook derives the 9 flow equations of the shallow-water DE4plus \
ansatz (two scalars H, Psi with response fields Hbar, Psibar), the case \
DE4plus_fast.wl was written for. Every step returns an immutable stage and \
prints a summary card: one PASS line per check, the warnings and the \
assumptions. A failed check prints a red FAIL block and stops the evaluation. \
Full expressions are shown only on request, with the Show... commands. The \
modules are described in docs/MODULES.md, the conventions in \
docs/CONVENTIONS.md.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f410ac8-8062-4d64-a729-59a369400c55"],

Cell["Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3fa76023-8b92-4840-94b0-8af44d023b77"],

Cell["1. Fields and ansatz", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7e2e1cb4-94d3-4d5a-935a-a33a775f4e0f"],

Cell["\<\
DefineTheory creates a response field <name>bar for each scalar. The ansatz \
is the action density, written with the package's own derivatives dt, grad, \
div, lap (not the System Dt, Grad: Dt[nk H] would add Dt[nk] terms). The \
parser prints the table of parsed monomials so that you can check it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4dbfea0-bde8-4331-9d57-117904f0c84f"],

Cell["\<\
theory = DefineTheory[\"Scalars\" -> {H, Psi}, \"Dimension\" -> Dim]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0cc8582f-b617-4b68-808d-ce61afb27ce2"],

Cell["\<\
ansatz = DefineAnsatz[theory, \"Density\" ->
    Hbar (dt[H] - nk Ak lap[H] + Hk lk lap[Psi] + lk div[H grad[Psi]])
  + Psibar (dt[Psi] - nk ank lap[Psi] + gk H - g2k lap[H] + lk/2 \
grad[Psi].grad[Psi])
  - Dhk aDhk grad[Hbar].grad[Hbar] - Dphik aDphik Psibar^2 - Dphik D2phik \
grad[Psibar].grad[Psibar] + Kk grad[Hbar].grad[Psibar],
  \"Couplings\" -> {nk, Ak, Hk, lk, ank, gk, g2k, Dhk, aDhk, Dphik, aDphik, \
D2phik, Kk}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b560181f-9df6-4a7b-8675-b37e3f6b2cbc"],

Cell["2. Vertices, regulator, propagator", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d6938f5f-d193-45b0-87b8-47cbbd4b110a"],

Cell["\<\
BuildVertices prints every Fourier vertex under the convention header (dt -> \
+I w, grad -> -I q, all momenta incoming, last leg = minus the sum of the \
others). The regulator entries are the amounts added to Gamma2_ab, including \
the 2 of a diagonal pair; the shapes stay abstract functions of y = q^2/k^2. \
The propagator is inverted in abstract atoms; Delta is the determinant whose \
roots are the poles, and its validity conditions say when they are causal \
(upper half w-plane).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff59f6ff-0eed-4a65-b15e-33ce947762e2"],

Cell["vertices = BuildVertices[ansatz];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"10b093ea-18a9-43d8-83dd-e230c8e40477"],

Cell["\<\
regulator = DefineRegulator[ansatz,
  {Hbar, H} -> nk q^2 arnh[q^2/k^2], {Psibar, Psi} -> nk q^2 arnphi[q^2/k^2],
  {Hbar, Hbar} -> -2 Dhk q^2 armh[q^2/k^2], {Psibar, Psibar} -> -2 Dphik \
armphi[q^2/k^2],
  \"Shapes\" -> {arnh, arnphi, armh, armphi}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"62840225-f4f1-42ed-af79-01de04d77489"],

Cell["prop = BuildPropagator[vertices, regulator];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3a7e9081-2a59-46df-9876-7de50e0c2162"],

Cell["3. Symmetries: what flows, what must not, what is dropped", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c45b9846-5d76-4a45-8595-4ae793e11d1f"],

Cell["\<\
Every monomial (I w)^m (q^2)^n of every Gamma2 entry up to the truncation \
orders gets a class: declared in the ansatz (it gets an equation), Protected \
(a symmetry forbids it, so its flow is checked to vanish), Neglected \
(computed, reported, dropped), or zero by structure. An untagged monomial \
stops the evaluation. Ward identities are assumed through the Protected tags, \
not derived.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3b2365e-e09b-4f17-a68d-9691aef8766a"],

Cell["\<\
symmetries = DeclareSymmetries[ansatz,
  Protected[{Hbar, _}, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \"Hbar -> Hbar + c(t) \
(mass conservation)\"],
  Protected[{Psi, _}, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \"Psi -> Psi + \
c(t)\"],
  Neglected[{H, Psibar}, \"Frequency\" -> {1, 2}, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\
\" -> \"truncation, z = 1 power counting\"],
  Neglected[{Psibar, Psibar}, \"Frequency\" -> 2, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\
\" -> \"coloured forcing, dropped\"],
  Neglected[_, \"Frequency\" -> {1, 2}, \"Momentum\" -> 1, \"Reason\" -> \
\"mixed i w q^2 / w^2 q^2 terms, dropped\"],
  NonRenormalised[lk, \"Reason\" -> \"Galilean invariance\"],
  \"TruncationOrders\" -> <|\"Frequency\" -> 2, \"Momentum\" -> 1|>];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fc1548e2-a411-45d1-a15b-7f386f3624d1"],

Cell["4. Loops, projection, frequency integrals, closure", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bb0f95a6-941b-4052-bc71-f5d7e0272f4d"],

Cell["\<\
The one-loop integrand of d_s Gamma2 is projected on each monomial at zero \
external frequency and momentum, then integrated over the loop frequency \
exactly by residues (no square roots: the result is rational in the \
coefficients of Delta). CheckClosure asserts the vanishing flows and turns \
each declared monomial into d_s(combination) = RHS, the number in front of \
the coefficient (e.g. the -2 of -2 Dhk aDhk) being divided out.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40776454-96cb-49ef-a801-09bf56ac0720"],

Cell["loops = BuildLoopIntegrands[vertices, prop, regulator];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fa0cc732-3682-4bdd-896c-ad007e71a3f9"],

Cell["projected = ProjectOnMonomials[loops, symmetries];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4d5be2e0-8a74-4f3e-803e-7d57f19e9cb7"],

Cell["integrated = IntegrateFrequencies[projected];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9091e77a-7c51-470c-8cc7-9b912c8dbff5"],

Cell["flows = CheckClosure[integrated, symmetries];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a3fd6665-9cd5-40d7-ba78-915e1e9623e8"],

Cell["ShowClosureReport[flows]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bce8540e-0271-455b-8990-d6134e9b13fc"],

Cell["5. Equations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fba84ed4-defc-4bb5-9ed7-253f6692d6b0"],

Cell["\<\
AssembleEquations writes each equation compactly in scale-stripped atoms \
(e.g. ScaleAtom[H, Hbar, 0, 0] = Ak + arnh[q^2/k^2]) and explicitly: the \
integrand of Int d^dq/(2 Pi)^d, with dsCoupling[c] = k dc/dk entering \
linearly and the shapes and their derivatives abstract. It takes about 35 s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79c0a608-e72b-45cf-9eac-86f1367a7d44"],

Cell["equations = AssembleEquations[flows];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"27b8dfc7-c251-49ac-8d68-1b65a897d727"],

Cell["ShowEquation[equations, gk]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"73b716ca-7232-4f3f-b58f-e9c488202986"],

Cell["ShowEquation[equations, Dhk aDhk]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"50f92c44-e8ea-482d-87be-841079d069a0"],

Cell["6. Numerical oracle", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"26bed8d3-b845-4cc7-ac97-195b2e14c48b"],

Cell["\<\
RunOracle recomputes every equation numerically at one random point, without \
the propagator algebra or the residues: matrix inverse of Gamma2 + R, \
numerical frequency integral, finite differences in the external frequency \
and momentum, in d = 2 and d = 3. It shares the vertices and the loop formula \
with the symbolic chain, so it does not test the loop normalisation; the KPZ \
notebook does.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6160efe2-cd90-42cc-b9d4-27b21d06265f"],

Cell["oracle = RunOracle[equations];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d508cc97-e31e-42ca-a811-2a18237b1b78"],

Cell["7. Saving", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4056f2e9-74df-48d9-bdd1-0bb10c4413ab"],

Cell["\<\
file = SaveStage[equations, FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \
\"swDE4plus-equations.wdx\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"636f0676-cae6-4fc4-8427-b38c7729f4a7"],

Cell["\<\
equations2 = LoadStage[file, \"Expect\" -> {theory, ansatz, regulator, \
symmetries}];
equations2 === equations\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"05f7b03e-79a0-4393-8de3-7e5f079acc2c"],

Cell["8. Dimensionless flows and the FlowRG file", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"29e4da64-8bec-4da8-84d7-2475ba20b677"],

Cell["\<\
DeriveDimensions derives the dimension of every coupling from the ansatz \
(Gamma_k is dimensionless), in the basis of k and N+1 = 3 reference \
couplings, and checks them (independent references, consistent monomials, \
action invariant under the derived rescaling). CheckDimensions compares hand \
values exactly. Here every reference appears only times an amplitude (nk ank, \
Dhk aDhk, Dphik aDphik); \"Mode\" -> \"Running\" makes each eta follow from \
that equation (the amplitude is counted as 1), the convention of the old \
hand-built export. Without it the eta would be fixed at run time (MUST_FIX).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe2a1c31-8fa0-48d3-9aec-aa4cc5f0970b"],

Cell["\<\
dims = DeriveDimensions[ansatz, \"References\" -> {Dphik -> {\"phi\", \
\"Mode\" -> \"Running\"}, Dhk -> {\"h\", \"Mode\" -> \"Running\"},
    nk -> {\"nu\", \"Mode\" -> \"Running\", \"Equation\" -> nk ank}}, \
\"Dimensionless\" -> {Ak, ank, aDhk, aDphik}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"111c59d4-5ac3-4510-b893-62ae56f5521a"],

Cell["\<\
CheckDimensions[dims, <|gk -> k Dphik^(1/2) Dhk^(-1/2) nk, lk -> k^(1 - \
Dim/2) Dphik^(-1/2) nk^(3/2), \"Frequency\" -> k^2 nk|>]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7de60d9e-9ef5-4ae1-a120-3e7617d1cd8d"],

Cell["\<\
AdimensionalEquations writes d_s chat = BetaL (not integrated) + Integral daq \
LoopMeasure BetaNL for each state coupling, and the linear system of the \
etas. Every beta is checked to be free of k and the references, structurally \
and by a random rescaling of the units. ExportJulia writes the FlowRG \
equations file for one d (this one uses r'', D2<shape>, which FlowRG must \
bind).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d4f2a46c-cd0f-4ce6-9f32-c38e6ea53779"],

Cell["\<\
adim = AdimensionalEquations[equations, dims, \"State\" -> {gk, g2k, lk, Hk, \
aDphik, D2phik, Kk, Ak, ank, aDhk}];
ShowBeta[adim, gk]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"91ca2e12-b89a-4a7a-8434-6cad9d499a18"],

Cell["\<\
ExportJulia[adim, \"Dimension\" -> 2, \"File\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"swDE4plus\", \"Equations2D.jl\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"612329ce-c02a-4d20-b08d-4be775820c9f"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"9183c8b4-822c-43b7-bc9c-2384501bdac9"
]
